<===> README.md
The built-in `if()` function, used when it is called via `meta.call()`,
must return `$if-false` for a falsy condition (it returned the condition).
<===>
================================================================================
<===> call/input.scss
@use "sass:meta";
a {
  b: meta.call(meta.get-function("if"), false, 1, 2);
  c: meta.call(meta.get-function("if"), true, 1, 2);
  d: meta.call(meta.get-function("if"), null, a, b);
  e: meta.call(meta.get-function("if"), $condition: false, $if-true: x, $if-false: y);
  f: call(get-function("if"), 0, yes, no);
  g: if(false, 1, 2);
}
<===> call/output.css
a {
  b: 2;
  c: 1;
  d: b;
  e: y;
  f: yes;
  g: 2;
}
